    "prompt": "Mode: reference-to-video. \n@image1 is the location — the room interior. Its architecture,\nmaterials, furniture, window and mirror placement come from @image1 and stay unchanged in\nevery frame; the room must be clearly visible and recognizable in the shot. \n@image2 is the only source of appearance — face, hair, build, outfit and its fit come from @image2 and stay\nunchanged in every frame. Neither the appearance nor the interior is described in text.\n\nConcept: someone is secretly filming from a window across the street. One continuous ~12s\ntake. Through the panoramic glass of the room from @image1, the person from @image2 is\nfooling around in front of the mirror — dancing, rolling the hips, laughing at themselves.\nThen they notice they are being watched, smile, walk to the window and pull the curtain.\n\nLook: bright daytime, high sun, clear sky. Amateur handheld footage — shot by an ordinary\nperson hiding in the building opposite, on a phone or small camera. Visible hand shake,\nimperfect framing, autofocus hunting, glare and reflections on the glass, slightly blown\nhighlights. No film crew, no cinematic polish, no camera move a real person could not do by\nhand.\n\n12 seconds, single continuous take, no cuts. Luxury hotel glass facade with many\npanoramic windows and balconies — the camera settles on one of them. The room from @image1\nis the one behind that glass.\n\n[0:00–0:03] From outside: the glass facade in bright daylight, many windows, balconies. The\nhandheld camera is aimed at the facade and clumsily zooms in toward the window where the\nperson from @image2 is visible inside — the room from @image1 clearly readable through the\nglass behind them. Camera: shaky handheld zoom, framing wanders before it settles, autofocus\nhunts, sun glare and reflections slide across the glass. Light: bright day, warm sun, crisp\nshadows inside the room.\n[0:03–0:07.5] Key scene: the zoom stops, the window sits in frame with only the small shake\nof a hand holding a camera. The person from @image2 goofs around in front of the full-length\nmirror — dancing to music, rhythmically rolling the hips, playfully turning their back to the\nmirror, a light playful twerk, laughing, adjusting the hair, checking themselves out, turning\nto profile and back. Movements loose, playful, at-home — the way girls fool around in front\nof guys. Camera: handheld, window held in frame, small constant shake. Light: unchanged,\nsunlight in the room.\n[0:07.5–0:10] The dance stops — the person from @image2 freezes, turns the head toward the\nwindow, realizes they are being watched. A slow smile spreads, the body turns to face the\nglass, direct eye contact into the camera, unbroken. Camera: handheld, window centered, small\nshake. Light: unchanged.\n[0:10–0:12] The person from @image2 walks up to the window, still holding eye contact, takes\nthe curtain and pulls it shut in one quick movement. Final frame is the closed curtain with\nbright daylight leaking around its edges. Camera: handheld, no pull-back, final frame held to\nthe end. Light: daylight under the curtain.\n\nAudio: daytime city ambience, distant street noise, muffled music from the room, laughter,\nfabric rustle, curtain sliding on the rod. No dialogue.\n\nLocks: keep the interior, architecture, window and mirror placement from @image1; keep\nidentity, hair, proportions and outfit from @image2; keep the secret observation angle from\nacross the street and the handheld shake throughout. No cuts or angle changes, no second\ncharacter, no text, logos or subtitles, no cinematic lighting, no stabilized or motorized\ncamera."
