    "prompt": "TASK\nRemake @video1 by replacing the main character with the person shown in @image1, replacing the revealed car with the vehicle shown in @image2\n\nPreserve the source duration, aspect ratio, performance, camera movement, framing, focus changes, editing and reveal timing.\n\nREFERENCES\n@video1 = authoritative source for action, gestures, expressions, lip-sync, card handling, vehicle reveal, camera and environment.\n\n@image1 = replacement character identity, body proportions, hairstyle, clothing, footwear and accessories. Completely replace the original character’s visible appearance, including face, hair, neck, body, hands and clothing. Do not transfer the reference background, pose, lighting or unrelated objects.\n\n@image2 = replacement vehicle identity. Preserve its recognizable silhouette, proportions, paint, wheels, headlights, windows and distinctive exterior details. Do not inherit the original car’s blue-and-white graphics unless independently present in \n@image2. Do not transfer reference people, background or lighting.\n\nCHARACTER REPLACEMENT\nUse ONE consistent replacement character throughout.\n\nPreserve the original performance: approaching the camera, showing the cards, lowering them, looking toward the car and reacting. Match the original body movement, facial-expression timing and lip-sync while retaining the replacement identity.\n\nIDENTICAL CARD DESIGN — SHARED MASTER\nCreate ONE master card design and apply an exact duplicate to BOTH physical cards.\n\nVEHICLE REPLACEMENT & REVEAL\nReplace the original car completely with the vehicle from @image2.\n\nThe replacement car FIRST appears at the exact moment the original vehicle is revealed after the card display. Keep the opening background free of the car wherever it is absent in the source.\n\nPreserve the source vehicle’s position, orientation and relationship to the character. Retain the replacement model’s natural proportions rather than stretching it into the original silhouette.\n\nOnce revealed, keep the same replacement vehicle consistent throughout all subsequent views. Where the source car is parked, the replacement stays parked. Add no driving, flight or transformation.\n\nCAMERA & ENVIRONMENT\nReproduce only the camera views that exist in @video1. Preserve the card close-up, foreground occlusion, focus transition back to the character and subsequent vehicle framing.\n\nKeep the original nighttime paved location, background structures and lighting. Do not import environments from either image reference.\n\nAdd no new angles, artificial zooms, reaction shots, transitions or cuts. Preserve existing cuts at their source timestamps.\n\nPHYSICAL & VISUAL INTEGRATION\nMatch source perspective, light direction, shadows, reflections, depth of field and motion blur.\n\nKeep realistic skin, hair, fabric, vehicle materials and stable geometry.\n\nAUDIO\nPreserve the original soundtrack, speech and timing. Match the replacement character’s lip movements to the original speech.\n\nAdd no new dialogue, music or background noise. Any visible card-handling sounds remain synchronized with the source action.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\nExactly one replacement character, one replacement vehicle and TWO identical cards.\n\nNo identity blending, duplicated people, original-character remnants, malformed hands, extra fingers, additional cards, differing card values, green-and-white print, vehicle morphing or reference-background transfer.\n\nDo not reveal the car prematurely. No additional captions, logos or watermarks.\n\nFINAL RESULT\nThe source performance and reveal remain intact, starring the character from @image1 and the vehicle from @image2. "
